From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:44:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D202 server: non-numeric stats ranges are rejected with 400

Upstream: GET /api/experimental/session/stats?from=yesterday answers 500 with an empty body. The from and to
query parameters decode with NumberFromString, which accepts NaN, and building the response range from NaN throws
"Invalid date".
Fixed: from and to decode with FiniteFromString, so a non-numeric or non-finite value is a 400 InvalidRequestError
(kind Query, "Expected a finite number"), like every other malformed query parameter.
Scenarios: session-api-transfer.test.ts "session statistics over imported history"
Upstream tests: none changed

diff --git a/packages/protocol/src/groups/session.ts b/packages/protocol/src/groups/session.ts
index 1bd0c70d34..0cad8c00c9 100644
--- a/packages/protocol/src/groups/session.ts
+++ b/packages/protocol/src/groups/session.ts
@@ -145,8 +145,8 @@ export const makeSessionGroup = <I extends HttpApiMiddleware.AnyId, S, FormI ext
     .add(
       HttpApiEndpoint.get("session.stats", "/api/experimental/session/stats", {
         query: Schema.Struct({
-          from: Schema.NumberFromString.pipe(Schema.optional),
-          to: Schema.NumberFromString.pipe(Schema.optional),
+          from: Schema.FiniteFromString.pipe(Schema.optional),
+          to: Schema.FiniteFromString.pipe(Schema.optional),
           project: Project.ID.pipe(Schema.optional),
           timezone: Schema.String.pipe(Schema.optional),
           tools: SessionStats.ToolMode.pipe(Schema.optional),
